From: JiaY-shi <shi05275@163.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: pcs: mtk_usxgmii: keep fixed 10G switch trunks out of autonegotiation

A fixed 10G USXGMII link to an external switch, such as the YT9224 CPU
port on the GL.iNet GL-BE14000, has no link partner to negotiate with.
Boards that mark the PCS with mediatek,force-fixed-10g get USXGMII
autonegotiation disabled and rate update mode selected instead.

This is the pcs_config part of the YT9224 series on OpenWrt main. The
rest of its PCS rework - link polling and CTLE checks - is not carried:
the 6.12 driver already reconfigures the PCS on link up and re-runs the
configuration from its polled get_state until the link comes back.

Signed-off-by: JiaY-shi <shi05275@163.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/pcs/pcs-mtk-usxgmii.c
+++ b/drivers/net/pcs/pcs-mtk-usxgmii.c
@@ -127,7 +127,17 @@ static int mtk_usxgmii_pcs_config(struct phylink_pcs *pcs, unsigned int neg_mode
 	bool mode_changed = false;
 
 	if (interface == PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_USXGMII) {
-		an_ctrl = FIELD_PREP(USXGMII_AN_SYNC_CNT, 0x1FF) | USXGMII_AN_ENABLE;
+		an_ctrl = FIELD_PREP(USXGMII_AN_SYNC_CNT, 0x1FF);
+
+		/* A fixed 10G USXGMII trunk to an external switch, such as
+		 * the YT9224 CPU port on the GL.iNet GL-BE14000, has no
+		 * link partner to negotiate with.
+		 */
+		if (!of_property_read_bool(mpcs->dev->of_node,
+					   "mediatek,force-fixed-10g"))
+			an_ctrl |= USXGMII_AN_ENABLE;
+		else
+			adapt_mode = USXGMII_RATE_UPDATE_MODE;
 		link_timer = FIELD_PREP(USXGMII_LINK_TIMER_IDLE_DETECT, 0x7B) |
 			     FIELD_PREP(USXGMII_LINK_TIMER_COMP_ACK_DETECT, 0x7B) |
 			     FIELD_PREP(USXGMII_LINK_TIMER_AN_RESTART, 0x7B);
